{"The new cleanup paths log every batch at error level including full ID lists (`r.log.Error(\"Annotations to clean...\", \"ids\", ids, ...)`), which will be very noisy and potentially huge in production": 0.9657831788063049, "Changing the cleanup ticker interval from 10 minutes to 1 minute in `CleanUpService.Run` substantially increases how often all cleanup jobs run - needs verification this is intentional for all environments and not just for testing or debugging": 0.9245427250862122, "`untilDoneOrCancelled` never stops when a batch returns zero affected rows - when `batchWork` returns `0, nil`, the loop continues and spins until the context is cancelled, wasting CPU instead of stopping when no work remains": 0.9200180768966675}